  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Chromyl chloride dissolves in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> solution to give a yellow solution. The chromate solution changes to blue colour chromium peroxide with hydrogen peroxide.</p><p>The reaction will be as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msup><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Hence, option A is the answer.</p><p> </p></blockquote>",
